From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:14:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(scores): a 0-10 mark for every workout and for every
 whole meal

Workouts: the energy estimate now also returns a 0-10 score of how good and
healthy the session was for this person that day (volume and intensity for
their recovery and goals, balance, rest, nothing risky) with one short reason;
shown in the workout detail and given to the coach.

Meals: marked as a whole meal (breakfast, mid-morning, lunch, snack, dinner,
nibbles), never photo by photo, since a first photo is often only part of it.
A meal is scored once it is over (its time slot has passed or a later meal of
the day is logged) and again only when it changes. Scoring runs when the Food
tab or the Today food card shows, for today and yesterday, with the foods,
the rest of the day and, under the coach's consent, profile, scale and goals.
The mark sits on the meal header (tap for the reason) and reaches the coach.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
